{
	title: 'Literal !!START blocks: tool arguments need no quoting or escaping',
	spec: "Every tool argument that carries text (BASH commands and scripts, EVAL code, regexes, GREP patterns, SEND messages, COMPACT summaries, SPAWN tasks, NOTIFY text, BRAVE queries) reaches the tool byte-exact as written; nothing needs quoting or escaping. The advertised form is a header line, TOOL [/* purpose */] [short arguments] [{ options }], followed by one raw block: a !!START line, literal lines, a !!END line. Prompts, HELP and examples advertise only this form for a tool's text field, even for one-liners; quoted strings stay accepted but unadvertised. The tool's syntax.block names the field the block fills; a call with marker lines is read by the generic grammar even when the tool has its own resolve, except EDIT. Block content excludes the newline (LF or CRLF) before !!END and keeps every other character, leading spaces and blank lines. A content line that is itself a marker takes one extra ! (!!!END writes a literal !!END). Command splitting never splits inside a block, for any tool; EVAL without a block keeps its code-to-the-end rule (task v99), unadvertised. EDIT keeps its own !!OLD/!!NEW/!!END grammar and is the only tool with several blocks. Malformed framing fails as a tool error showing the raw text, and nothing runs; each failure carries a code quirks (task hq6) can recognize: block-unclosed, block-nested, block-two, block-new (lone !!NEW, which quirks accept in place of !!START), block-old (!!OLD outside EDIT, rejected), block-stray-end; a block for a tool without syntax.block fails too. SYSTEM.md drops its JS-string-literal and backslash rule and teaches blocks for text arguments.",
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'User, 2026-11-16: every frontier model breaks JS string escaping in tool calls. Seen with Claude Fable 5.2 (high effort): a heredoc inside a BASH string turned \\n into a real newline; a rewrite then lost backslashes, breaking \\d in a regex. Models burn turns fixing escapes instead of working. The agent writing this task hit it too: tsk add through BASH doubled every backslash.',
		'User, 2026-11-19: COMPACT nearly always fails; models struggle with quoted JS strings nested inside their JSON tool calls. Tool calls should use heredoc-style literal blocks instead. EVAL (2026-11-19) takes its code as literal text to the end of the cmd.',
		"User, 2026-11-19: advertise only the block form for a tool's main text field, even for one-liners (BASH, EVAL, SEND, COMPACT ...); quoted strings stay accepted but never appear in prompts, HELP or examples. Goal: the least possible quoting.",
